From c8706b4ce7cfec250a9c20268d4854e50c8e35c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Bangert <100193+bbangert@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] soc: rockchip: power-domain: fail a domain power-up
 instead of panicking

A power domain whose bus never acks the de-idle request, or whose status
never reads on, panics the kernel unless pm_domains.always_on is set. On
a board whose rail is still off when a consumer attaches (an NPU whose
supply the boot loader leaves off), that is a reset loop that only a
serial console could explain.

Panic only when powering down, where the driver has no way back. A
failed power-up now returns its error, which genpd turns into
-EPROBE_DEFER for the consumer. After a failed de-idle the domain is
idled and switched off again: rockchip_pd_power() skips the sequence when
the status bit already reads on, so leaving it on would let the next
attempt hand the consumer an idle bus whose first access hangs.

pm_domains.always_on is not used instead: it also keeps every domain on
for good and leaves that idle-bus retry in place.
---
 drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c b/drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c
index fee0db1..4f48d9c 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/rockchip/pm_domains.c
@@ -677,7 +677,12 @@ static int rockchip_pmu_set_idle_request(struct rockchip_pm_domain *pd,
 
 	return ret;
 error:
-	if (!pm_domain_always_on)
+	/*
+	 * A failed de-idle (power-up) is backed out by rockchip_pd_power()
+	 * and fails the consumer's probe; only a domain that cannot be idled
+	 * for power-down is unrecoverable.
+	 */
+	if (idle && !pm_domain_always_on)
 		panic("panic_on_set_idle set ...\n");
 	return ret;
 }
@@ -1095,7 +1100,8 @@ static int rockchip_do_pmu_set_power_domain(struct rockchip_pm_domain *pd,
 	return ret;
 
 error:
-	if (!pm_domain_always_on)
+	/* A domain that never reports on just fails its consumer's probe. */
+	if (!on && !pm_domain_always_on)
 		panic("panic_on_set_domain set ...\n");
 	return ret;
 }
@@ -1168,6 +1174,14 @@ static int rockchip_pd_power(struct rockchip_pm_domain *pd, bool power_on)
 			if (ret) {
 				dev_err(pd->pmu->dev, "failed to set deidle request '%s',\n",
 					genpd->name);
+				/*
+				 * Power back off: with the status bit left on, the
+				 * next attempt would skip this sequence and report
+				 * an idle bus as usable, hanging its first access.
+				 */
+				rockchip_pmu_set_idle_request(pd, true);
+				rockchip_pmu_mem_shut_down(pd, true);
+				rockchip_do_pmu_set_power_domain(pd, false);
 				goto out;
 			}
 
